    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.learning_content_registry_items, $seed${"service_key":"grammar","content_type":"grammar.unit","source_table":"grammar_units","source_ref":"a2-ready-or-bored-participle-adjectives","title":"Bored or boring? Adjectives for feelings and causes","skill_key":"grammar","cefr_level":"A2","difficulty":0.3,"status":"published","description":"Use the -ed adjective to say how someone feels. If a girl wants to learn more about birds, she is interested in birds. If a boy has nothing to do and wants to leave, he is bored. If he cannot wait for his first boat ride, he is excited about it. If he sees something he did not expect, he is surprised.\n\nUse the -ing adjective to describe what causes the feeling. A book about birds can be interesting, a long wait can be boring, a boat ride can be exciting, and an unexpected result can be surprising. A person can cause the feeling too. A guide who tells stories that make people want to hear more is an interesting person.\n\nThis pattern works for the four pairs here. Other adjectives have their own meanings. For example, a broken cup has a crack or is in pieces. Broken describes the cup's condition.","subskill_keys":["grammar.accuracy","grammar.ed-ing-adjectives","grammar.transfer"],"estimated_minutes":8,"learning_objective":"The visitor is interested because she wants to hear more. The guide is interesting because his stories make her want to hear more.","tags":["A2","participle-adjectives","feelings","ed-ing-adjectives"],"payload_json":{"focus_area":"ed-ing-adjectives","common_error_pattern":"Learners sometimes choose the ending based on whether the subject is a person or a thing. For these pairs, choose -ed for the person who feels something and -ing for whoever or whatever causes the feeling.","examples":[{"bad":"Context: The reader wants to learn more. The reader is interesting in the story.","good":"The reader is interested in the story."},{"bad":"Context: The speech makes everyone lose interest. The speech is bored.","good":"The speech is boring."},{"bad":"Context: The children cannot wait to play. The children are exciting about the game.","good":"The children are excited about the game."},{"bad":"Context: Nobody expected the team to win. The result was surprised.","good":"The result was surprising."}]}}$seed$::jsonb) r
