    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.learning_content_registry_items, $seed${"service_key":"grammar","content_type":"grammar.unit","source_table":"grammar_units","source_ref":"b1-each-every-and-all-in-a-round","title":"Each, every and all in a workshop round","skill_key":"grammar","cefr_level":"B1","difficulty":0.45,"status":"published","description":"Use each or every before a singular count noun. Each participant gets a turn puts the focus on one person at a time. Every participant gets a turn makes clear that nobody is left out. Both sentences can describe the same workshop rule. Choose each if you want readers to think about people individually, and every if you want to stress that the rule covers everyone.\n\nUse all before a plural noun to refer to the whole group. All participants clap together describes a group action. All participants get a turn can also describe something people do separately. The rest of the sentence tells you how the group takes part.\n\nWhen you name a specific group, you can say each of the participants or all of the participants. Use each of them or all of them when the group is already clear. With each of, the subject takes a singular verb: Each of them has a turn. To use every with of, say every one of th","subskill_keys":["grammar.accuracy","grammar.each-every-all","grammar.transfer"],"estimated_minutes":8,"learning_objective":"Each speaker gets a different question focuses on the question given to each person. Every speaker must answer a question stresses that the rule has no exceptions. All speakers read the final line together refers to the group doing one action together. Each and every can both fit many workshop rules, so pay attention to the focus or the form the task asks for.","tags":["each-every-and-all","workshop-participation"],"payload_json":{"focus_area":"each-every-all","common_error_pattern":"Use each or every with a singular count noun and all with a plural count noun in these patterns. Use each of or all of before an object pronoun such as them. If you use every with of, include one.","examples":[{"bad":"Each learners receives a cue card.","good":"Each learner receives a cue card."},{"bad":"Every groups gets a chance to lead.","good":"Every group gets a chance to lead."},{"bad":"All observer raise their hands together.","good":"All observers raise their hands together."},{"bad":"Each them has a turn at the microphone.","good":"Each of them has a turn at the microphone."}]}}$seed$::jsonb) r
