    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.grammar_units, $seed${"slug":"b1-future-time-clauses-at-a-checkpoint","title":"Future time clauses at an outdoor club checkpoint","level":"B1","status":"published","sort_order":390,"metadata":{},"focus_area":"future-time-clauses","explanation_text":"When you plan an outdoor club visit, use the present simple in a time clause that tells you when a future action will happen. Start the time clause with when, as soon as, until, once, before, or after. Use will plus the base form of the verb in the main clause: We will hand out maps when the group arrives. If the time clause comes first, put a comma after it: When the group arrives, we will hand out maps.\n\nUse before and after to show the order of two actions. As soon as means that the next action will happen immediately. Once shows that one thing must happen first. Until marks the point when an action or situation ends.\n\nWhen can also introduce an embedded question about a future time: Do you know when the ranger will arrive? Here, when the ranger will arrive is what you want to find out. In We'll start when the ranger arrives, the when clause tells you when we'll start. In this lesson, the examples mostly use will in the main clause. An instruction can also combine with a future time clause: “Call me when you arrive.”","contrast_text":"We'll call the ranger when the gate opens. The when clause tells us when we'll call. We'll ask when the gate will open. The when clause gives the question we'll ask: What time will the gate open?","common_error_pattern":"Putting will in an ordinary future time clause or using question word order in an embedded question. Write We'll wait until the fog clears and Do you know when the fog will clear?","examples_json":[{"bad":"We'll unlock the equipment shed when the caretaker will get here.","good":"We'll unlock the equipment shed when the caretaker gets here."},{"bad":"As soon as the wind drop, we'll put up the shelter.","good":"As soon as the wind drops, we'll put up the shelter."},{"bad":"We'll keep the side path closed until the ground will dry.","good":"We'll keep the side path closed until the ground dries."},{"bad":"Do you know when will the water station open?","good":"Do you know when the water station will open?"}],"tags":["future-time-clauses","outdoor-club","when-clauses"]}$seed$::jsonb) r
    returning id into v_parent_id;
