    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.grammar_units, $seed${"slug":"b1-like-and-as-for-roles-and-similarity","title":"Like and as at the maker festival","level":"B1","status":"published","sort_order":410,"metadata":{},"focus_area":"like-and-as-for-similarity-and-role","explanation_text":"Use like before a noun phrase to show that two people or things are similar in some way. In a note to volunteers, “The paper lantern opens like an umbrella” compares the way the two objects open. Use as before a noun phrase to name someone’s actual role or explain what something is used for. In “I’m here as a guide,” guide is your role. In “We use a toolbox lid as a tray,” the lid has the function of a tray during the activity.\n\nUse as before a clause to show how to do something. “Set up the stand as the diagram shows” tells volunteers to follow the diagram. In “Do as shown,” as shown is a shorter form of as it is shown. In informal conversation, you may also hear like before a clause, as in “Set it up like I showed you.” For the written festival instructions in this lesson, choose as before a clause that tells someone how to do a task.","contrast_text":"“She works as a guide” names her actual job. “She speaks like a guide” compares the way she speaks with the way a guide speaks. “She speaks as the trainer showed her” says she follows the trainer’s example.","common_error_pattern":"Using like to name an assigned role or function, or using as before a noun phrase when the intended meaning is a simple comparison.","examples_json":[{"bad":"I’m on duty like a safety checker. (My assigned role is safety checker.)","good":"I’m on duty as a safety checker."},{"bad":"The thin metal strip bends as a spring. (The strip bends in a similar way to a spring.)","good":"The thin metal strip bends like a spring."},{"bad":"This wooden crate serves like a seat. (The crate is the seat at this station.)","good":"This wooden crate serves as a seat."},{"bad":"Join the two parts as the label show.","good":"Join the two parts as the label shows."}],"tags":["like-and-as","similarity","roles-and-functions","manner","maker-festival"]}$seed$::jsonb) r
