    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.grammar_units, $seed${"slug":"b1-present-perfect-continuous-in-a-team-log","title":"Present perfect continuous in a team log","level":"B1","status":"published","sort_order":360,"metadata":{},"focus_area":"present-perfect-continuous","explanation_text":"A community newsletter team log can show how long a job has been in progress or how many things the team has finished. To focus on an activity that is still going on, use the present perfect continuous: have or has + been + the -ing form. For example, “We have been sorting reader letters for an hour” tells the team how long the sorting has been going on. Use for with a length of time and since with a starting point.\n\nTo record a completed count up to now, use the present perfect simple: have or has + the past participle. “We have sorted twelve reader letters so far” gives the number of letters already sorted. The team may still have more letters to sort. Some verbs describe states, such as know. Use the simple form for a state that is still true: “I have known our editor since May.”","contrast_text":"“We have been checking addresses for an hour” reports the duration of work that is still in progress. “We have checked twenty addresses so far” reports how many checks are complete.","common_error_pattern":"Use have or has + been + the -ing form for ongoing work. Use have or has + the past participle to report a completed count or an ongoing state with know.","examples_json":[{"bad":"The layout team has been adjust the margins for half an hour.","good":"The layout team has been adjusting the margins for half an hour."},{"bad":"We have wrote four teasers for the front page so far.","good":"We have written four teasers for the front page so far."},{"bad":"Lena has been spoke to a local baker since ten o’clock, and the interview is still going.","good":"Lena has been speaking to a local baker since ten o’clock, and the interview is still going."},{"bad":"I have been knowing our volunteer illustrator since March.","good":"I have known our volunteer illustrator since March."}],"tags":["b1","present-perfect-continuous","present-perfect-simple","duration","completed-count","community-newsletter"]}$seed$::jsonb) r
