    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.learning_content_registry_items, $seed${"service_key":"grammar","content_type":"grammar.unit","source_table":"grammar_units","source_ref":"b1-tell-and-ask-with-an-infinitive","title":"Reporting commands and requests with told and asked","skill_key":"grammar","cefr_level":"B1","difficulty":0.45,"status":"published","description":"When you pass on an instruction, name the person who gave it and the person who received it. For a command, use told + person + to + base verb. For a polite request, use asked + person + to + base verb. For example, if Omar says to Nina, “Could you check the microphone, please?” you can report it as “Omar asked Nina to check the microphone.”\n\nFor a negative instruction, this lesson uses not to + base verb: “Omar told Nina not to move the microphone.” You can also use asked + person + not to for a polite request. Keep the receiver between told or asked and the infinitive. If you are Nina and you tell a teammate what Omar said to you, use me: “Omar told me not to move the microphone.” Me shows who received the instruction.","subskill_keys":["grammar.accuracy","grammar.reported-requests-and-instructions","grammar.transfer"],"estimated_minutes":8,"learning_objective":"In the studio, Kai says directly to Lena, “Lock the equipment cabinet.” Later, Lena messages Sam, their studio teammate: “Kai told me to lock the equipment cabinet.” In Lena’s message, me refers to Lena, who received the instruction.","tags":["reported-commands","reported-requests","to-infinitive","negative-infinitive"],"payload_json":{"focus_area":"reported-requests-and-instructions","common_error_pattern":"Keep the receiver after told or asked and before to or not to. Use an object form such as me or him. Follow to with the base verb.","examples":[{"bad":"The guide told us stay on the path.","good":"The guide told us to stay on the path."},{"bad":"The receptionist asked we to sign the visitor book.","good":"The receptionist asked us to sign the visitor book."},{"bad":"The instructor told the class not to touching the wet paint.","good":"The instructor told the class not to touch the wet paint."},{"bad":"Priya asked Ben to copies the link.","good":"Priya asked Ben to copy the link."}]}}$seed$::jsonb) r
