    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.grammar_units, $seed${"slug":"b2-reduced-relatives-in-event-notices","title":"Reduced defining relatives in event notices","level":"B2","status":"published","sort_order":410,"metadata":{},"focus_area":"reduced-relative-clauses","explanation_text":"A defining relative clause identifies which people or things a notice refers to. When the noun is doing something that is in progress at the relevant time, you can often replace who or that plus a progressive verb with an -ing form. In a live queue update, “people who are waiting outside” becomes “people waiting outside.” If the noun receives the action, use the past participle and keep details that identify the group. “Prints that were selected yesterday” becomes “prints selected yesterday.”\n\nCheck the noun’s role before you shorten the clause. In “the curator whom we invited,” we did the inviting. “The curator inviting us” reverses the roles, so keep the full relative clause if the notice needs to state who issued the invitation.\n\nA reduced defining relative sits after the noun it identifies. A clause such as “Leaving the hall, visitors picked up a programme” gives the circumstances of the main action. It tells us when visitors picked up a programme.","contrast_text":"“Visitors leaving the hall can collect a programme” identifies which visitors can collect one. “Leaving the hall, visitors picked up a programme” tells us when the visitors picked one up.","common_error_pattern":"Using -ing for a noun that receives the action, or dropping the subject of an object relative and changing who performs the action.","examples_json":[{"bad":"At the live check-in, guests are queuing at the side door should have their passes ready.","good":"At the live check-in, guests queuing at the side door should have their passes ready."},{"bad":"The photographs choose by the panel will appear in the foyer.","good":"The photographs chosen by the panel will appear in the foyer."},{"bad":"Intended meaning: the hosts thanked the donor. The donor thanking the hosts will open the reception.","good":"The donor whom the hosts thanked will open the reception."},{"bad":"Intended meaning: only spectators currently using the east exit should follow the blue arrows. Using the east exit, spectators should follow the blue arrows.","good":"Spectators using the east exit should follow the blue arrows."}],"tags":["reduced-defining-relatives","active-ing-relatives","passive-participle-relatives","object-relatives","event-notices"]}$seed$::jsonb) r
