    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.learning_content_registry_items, $seed${"service_key":"grammar","content_type":"grammar.unit","source_table":"grammar_units","source_ref":"b2-stative-and-active-meanings","title":"Stative and active meanings when planning a service","skill_key":"grammar","cefr_level":"B2","difficulty":0.6,"status":"published","description":"Choose the verb form by asking what the verb means in this sentence. In a service planning meeting, “I think the booking form is clear” gives an opinion. “I’m thinking about removing a question” describes an option under consideration. “We have two spare tablets” describes possession, while “We’re having a trial run” describes an activity. “I see why callers get confused” means I understand their problem, while “I’m seeing the reception manager tomorrow” describes an arranged meeting.\n\nWith taste and feel, notice who or what is doing the tasting or feeling. “The soup tastes salty” and “The strap feels rough” describe qualities. “The cook is tasting the soup” and “The designer is feeling the strap for a seam” describe deliberate checks. The present simple can also describe repeated actions, as in “The cook tastes every batch.” For personal sensations, both “I feel better” and “I’m feeling","subskill_keys":["grammar.accuracy","grammar.stative-and-dynamic-meanings","grammar.transfer"],"estimated_minutes":8,"learning_objective":"Use the present simple to state an opinion, describe possession, show understanding, or report a sensory quality. Use the present continuous for an activity in progress, such as weighing an option, holding a trial run, or sampling food, and for an arranged meeting. The present simple also works for habitual actions.","tags":["b2","stative-and-active-meanings","service-planning"],"payload_json":{"focus_area":"stative-and-dynamic-meanings","common_error_pattern":"A time cue such as right now can describe a current state as well as an ongoing action. For current possession, say “Right now, we have two spare tablets.” To report an activity in progress, say “Right now, we’re having a trial run.”","examples":[{"bad":"I’m thinking the larger sign is clearer. (Intended meaning: a settled opinion about the sign.)","good":"I think the larger sign is clearer."},{"bad":"We’re having three portable ramps in stock. (Intended meaning: current possession.)","good":"We have three portable ramps in stock."},{"bad":"I’m seeing what you mean about the pickup queue. (Intended meaning: I understand your point.)","good":"I see what you mean about the pickup queue."},{"bad":"The mint tea is tasting bitter. (Intended meaning: a general description of the recipe.)","good":"The mint tea tastes bitter."}]}}$seed$::jsonb) r
