    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.grammar_units, $seed${"slug":"b2-would-rather-and-would-prefer","title":"Would rather and would prefer","level":"B2","status":"published","sort_order":380,"metadata":{},"focus_area":"would-rather-and-would-prefer","explanation_text":"Use would rather + the base form when you are choosing what you want to do. In “I’d rather meet on Thursday,” the person with the preference and the person who will attend the meeting are the same. You can express that choice with would prefer + to + the base form: “I’d prefer to meet on Thursday.” In both patterns, ’d is short for would.\n\nTo express a preference about what someone else does, you can use would rather + subject + past simple. For example, “I’d rather Maya sent the draft tomorrow” means that you want Maya to send it tomorrow. Sent has the grammatical form of the past simple, but tomorrow gives the action a future time. The past form presents the action as something you want rather than as a report of a past event. Some speakers, especially in American English, use the base form here: “I’d rather Maya send the draft tomorrow.” In “Maya sent the draft yesterday,” the same verb form reports an actual past action.","contrast_text":"“We’d rather check the figures today” and “We’d prefer to check the figures today” both describe what we want to do. “We’d rather the finance team checked the figures today” gives the checking to the finance team. Checked is past in form, while today gives the preferred action its time.","common_error_pattern":"For your own action, put to after would prefer and use the bare verb after would rather. To practice the past-simple pattern for another person’s action, put the subject after would rather and then use the past simple.","examples_json":[{"bad":"I’d rather to chair the first session.","good":"I’d rather chair the first session."},{"bad":"Nina would prefer record the decisions herself.","good":"Nina would prefer to record the decisions herself."},{"bad":"We’d rather Omar will introduce the new reviewer tomorrow.","good":"We’d rather Omar introduced the new reviewer tomorrow."},{"bad":"They would rather the panel to read the summary before lunch.","good":"They would rather the panel read the summary before lunch."}],"tags":["would-rather","would-prefer","preference","modal-remoteness"]}$seed$::jsonb) r
