    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.learning_content_registry_items, $seed${"service_key":"grammar","content_type":"grammar.unit","source_table":"grammar_units","source_ref":"b2-would-was-going-to-and-was-about-to","title":"Would, was going to and was about to","skill_key":"grammar","cefr_level":"B2","difficulty":0.6,"status":"published","description":"All three forms let you look ahead from a point in the past. Use would + base verb for an event that lay ahead from that point. In a recap of the canceled load-in, “We soon realized the delay would affect the weekend shows” describes an expected consequence as it appeared then. The sentence leaves open whether the shows were actually affected.\n\nUse was or were going to + base verb for an intention or plan already in place. It can also express a prediction based on what was apparent at the time. “The crew were going to bring the flats through the side door” identifies the chosen route before the cancellation. Use was or were about to + base verb when an action was on the point of starting. “Mina was about to unlock the side door when the cancellation message arrived” places the interruption just before she started. A plan can also be about to happen. For planned actions, going to can high","subskill_keys":["grammar.accuracy","grammar.future-in-the-past","grammar.transfer"],"estimated_minutes":8,"learning_objective":"“The truck would arrive after rehearsal” looks ahead from a past viewpoint. “The driver was going to wait by the stage door” identifies the driver's plan. “The driver was about to pull away when the alert came through” puts the alert at the moment just before departure.","tags":["future-in-the-past","past-intentions","imminent-actions"],"payload_json":{"focus_area":"future-in-the-past","common_error_pattern":"Keep the past form of be before going to or about to, and match it to the subject. Use a base verb after would and after to in the other two forms.","examples":[{"bad":"We knew the road closure would blocked the delivery route.","good":"We knew the road closure would block the delivery route."},{"bad":"The volunteers was going to clear a path through the lobby.","good":"The volunteers were going to clear a path through the lobby."},{"bad":"The stage manager about to call the crew when the alert appeared.","good":"The stage manager was about to call the crew when the alert appeared."},{"bad":"The electrician had just reached for the test switch. At that moment she was about to test the work lights next week.","good":"The electrician had just reached for the test switch. She was about to test the work lights when the cancellation message arrived."}]}}$seed$::jsonb) r
