    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.grammar_units, $seed${"slug":"c1-particle-and-prepositional-verbs","title":"Particle placement in editorial and studio work","level":"C1","status":"published","sort_order":360,"metadata":{},"focus_area":"particle-and-prepositional-verb-order","explanation_text":"In this unit, use standard written British English and the meanings given here. In look up (find information), hand in (submit) and put off (postpone), the particle can follow the verb or a short noun phrase: look up the date or look the date up. With an unstressed object pronoun, place it between the verb and the particle: look it up.\n\nIn look into (investigate), refer to (direct readers to a source) and go over (review), keep the preposition before its object in the ordinary statements practised here. This order applies to noun phrases and pronouns alike: look into the discrepancy and look into it.\n\nWhen both particle positions are grammatical, place a long or structurally complex noun phrase after the particle in these exercises. This keeps the verb and particle together while readers process the details. In a formal submission notice, an editor may choose submit instead of hand in. That is a register choice. The placement rules still apply whenever you use hand in.","contrast_text":"Compare hand the proofs in and hand in the proofs with hand them in. With refer to, the order stays fixed in both refer to the proofs and refer to them. For a long object, prefer hand in the proofs with the final corrections from both reviewers.","common_error_pattern":"Place an unstressed object pronoun before a movable particle, as in put it off. When directing readers to a source with refer to, keep the source after to: refer to the style sheet.","examples_json":[{"bad":"The fact-checker looked up it before the caption went to press.","good":"The fact-checker looked it up before the caption went to press."},{"bad":"The trainee handed in them after the portfolio review.","good":"The trainee handed them in after the portfolio review."},{"bad":"The managing editor will look the discrepancy into before approving the proofs.","good":"The managing editor will look into the discrepancy before approving the proofs."},{"bad":"We went the revised opening over before recording the narration.","good":"We went over the revised opening before recording the narration."}],"tags":["particle-and-prepositional-verbs","particle-shifting","pronoun-placement","object-weight","register"]}$seed$::jsonb) r
