    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.learning_content_registry_items, $seed${"service_key":"grammar","content_type":"grammar.unit","source_table":"grammar_units","source_ref":"c1-tense-choices-in-an-observation-report","title":"Tense choices in an observation report","skill_key":"grammar","cefr_level":"C1","difficulty":0.75,"status":"published","description":"Choose the tense by asking what the sentence is doing in the report. Use the past simple to record a completed procedure or an event within a finished observation session. In “The observer reset the counter before the final trial,” the verb places the action in the documented sequence. When directing readers to a named visual included in the report, the present simple is a common choice. “Table 2 shows the distribution of response times” describes what readers can see on the page.\n\nThe present simple can also state what the evidence suggests at the time of writing. Use the present perfect when you frame earlier observations as part of an evidence record that extends to the time of writing. “The team has documented three recurrences so far” leaves the reporting period open. Tense conventions vary across disciplines, especially in results sections. A single paragraph can move from a comple","subskill_keys":["grammar.accuracy","grammar.tense-in-observation-reports","grammar.transfer"],"estimated_minutes":8,"learning_objective":"“The sensor registered a spike during the final trial” locates an event in a finished session. “Figure 4 shows the spike” directs readers to material in the report. “The pattern suggests a brief interruption” states the report's current interpretation. “The team has recorded two similar spikes so far” summarizes evidence gathered over a period that is still open.","tags":["tense-choices-in-an-observation-report","observation-reports","academic-writing"],"payload_json":{"focus_area":"tense-in-observation-reports","common_error_pattern":"Carrying the past tense from the methods section into a sentence intended as a present-tense guide to a figure, or using the present perfect for an event explicitly located in a finished observation period.","examples":[{"bad":"During yesterday's completed calibration session, the technician has adjusted the reference scale twice.","good":"During yesterday's completed calibration session, the technician adjusted the reference scale twice."},{"bad":"[Guiding the reader through the chart on this page in the present tense] Chart 3 displayed the readings by depth.","good":"[Guiding the reader through the chart on this page in the present tense] Chart 3 displays the readings by depth."},{"bad":"The difference between the two traces indicate a timing offset.","good":"The difference between the two traces indicates a timing offset."},{"bad":"So far in the ongoing survey, we have saw the same behaviour at three sites.","good":"So far in the ongoing survey, we have seen the same behaviour at three sites."}]}}$seed$::jsonb) r
