      r.skill_key, r.subskill_keys, r.cefr_level, r.difficulty, r.estimated_minutes, r.learning_objective, r.tags, r.status, r.payload_json,
      jsonb_build_object('seeded_by', v_seed)
    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.learning_content_registry_items, $seed${"service_key":"grammar","content_type":"grammar.unit","source_table":"grammar_units","source_ref":"c2-polarity-items-in-formal-critique","title":"Polarity items in formal critique","skill_key":"grammar","cefr_level":"C2","difficulty":0.9,"status":"published","description":"In a formal critique, polarity items help specify what the evidence fails to establish or what a reviewer is asking the authors to establish. In “The appendix does not provide any baseline estimates,” any falls within the scope of negation. In a direct question, “Did the panel ever test the threshold during the pilot?”, ever asks whether the test occurred on even one occasion within a closed period.\n\nAn explicit not is only one way to license these items. “The reviewers doubt that the adjustment had any effect at all” places any and at all inside the claim being doubted. “Hardly any submissions included a sensitivity analysis” uses the near-negative hardly. At all can sharpen the question of whether there was an effect to any degree.\n\nTemporal yet looks up to a reference point, such as the present in “Has the board responded yet?” In an affirmative rule, “Reviewers may inspect any file i","subskill_keys":["grammar.accuracy","grammar.negative-polarity-items","grammar.transfer"],"estimated_minutes":8,"learning_objective":"“The panel did not consult any external assessor” denies that an external consultation took place. “The panel may consult any external assessor on the register” makes each registered assessor eligible. The first is a claim about what happened, and the second is a statement of permission.","tags":["polarity-items","formal-critique","negation","direct-questions","free-choice-any"],"payload_json":{"focus_area":"negative-polarity-items","common_error_pattern":"Check where the polarity item sits relative to the question or negation. A negative phrase later in the sentence does not automatically license an earlier any. In a standard formal declarative intended to deny that any reports addressed an issue, use “No reports addressed it” or “The reports did not address it.”","examples":[{"bad":"Any of the submissions did not disclose a funding source. (Intended meaning: zero submissions disclosed one.)","good":"The submissions did not disclose any funding sources."},{"bad":"Did the contractor ever documented a calibration failure during the trial?","good":"Did the contractor ever document a calibration failure during the trial?"},{"bad":"The new weighting affected the final ranking at all. (An affirmative finding that the ranking changed.)","good":"The new weighting affected the final ranking."},{"bad":"The committee has already issued its response. (Status as of now: the response is still outstanding.)","good":"The committee has not issued its response yet."}]}}$seed$::jsonb) r
